_struct_biol.id                    1 
_struct_biol.details               
;THE MULTIMERIC STRUCTURES OF BACILLUS STEAROTHERMOPHILUS
LEUDH AND BACILLUS SUBTILIS HAVE BEEN REPORTED AS HEXAMERS
ON THE BASIS OF GEL FILTRATION STUDIES; INDEED THE LEUCINE
DEHYDROGENASE FROM BACILLUS SPHAERICUS WAS ALSO INITIALLY
REPORTED AS A HEXAMER.  HOWEVER THE X-RAY STRUCTURE IS MOST
DEFINITELY A HOMOOCTAMER AND ON THE BASIS OF THE SEQUENCE
IDENTITIES BETWEEN THE LEUDH'S FROM THE OTHER SPECIES,
THEN THESE MUST ALL BE OCTAMERS AS WELL.
;
